WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Jeff, wonderful to see you.
How are you?

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's very wonderful
to see you, Seth.

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I am...good,

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.608 line:92%
everything considered, you know.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.910 line:92%
My heart goes out to all those

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are not so fortunate,
of course,

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.915 line:92%
but, for now, we're okay.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm here with my family
in England.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're shootin'
that "Jurassic World" movi

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.855
and they've put their hear
and soul into the protocol

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:27.460
and we're safe and having
a creative blast, you know

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.128 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-That's really nice.

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:30.897
You were one of the first
productions to go back,

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:31.831 line:92%
the new "Jurassic Park" film

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think one of the thing
that was nice is not just

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.903 size:84% position:42%
the safety protocols
you were talking about,

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:39.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
but this is the first time
that you and Sam Neill

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:42.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Laura Dern
have been together

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.910 size:81% position:41% line:92%
for 30 years, correct?

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes!
That's right.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.113 line:92%
Our characters, certainly,

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
oh, we've been in touch
here and there.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But that's right.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
Our characters,
Sam Neill's character

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Laura Dern,
we're back together.

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:57.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
Colin Trevorrow,
great writer-director,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
is directing it.
He's fantastic.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, of course,
Chris Pratt is in it,

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.096 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Bryce Dallas Howard,

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.864 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and Mamoudou Athie,

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
DeWanda Wise,
BD Wong, Justice Smith.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:11.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a whole coterie
of luminaries.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
How do your children --

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know we have kids
that are of similar age.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are they enjoying
England, so far?

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.579 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, they are!

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:20.447 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They are.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:22.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course,
we have a very special

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
view of it right here,
but this is a great place.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.387 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They love it.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.255 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I'm around all the time.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And Emilie's mom

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.258 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is here, actually,

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:35.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so we've got lotsa --
It's very cozy.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.163 line:92%
And they're havin' a good time

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.032 line:92%
They're doin' all kinda --

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're just --
They're loving it.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:43.269 size:75% position:38% line:92%
They feed the ducks.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.237 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They touch cows.

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:46.239 line:92%
They were kind of -- Seth.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.041 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They feed donkeys.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.109 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They're good.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.910 line:92%
-That's wonderful to hear.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.678 line:92%
-I have a piano in my room

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:54.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Charlie's taking
piano lessons -- had been --

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:55.915 line:92%
but I'm taking him through

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not only do I do
my piano homework,

00:01:57.217 --> 00:02:01.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm taking him through his
Suzuki lesson every day.

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:02.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's proceeding apace.
-Now, tell me,

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
how young were you
when you started,

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.592 line:92%
when you got your first lesson

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:09.996
-I think, as I remembered,
ten-ish or nine-ish, or ten-ish.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.632 line:92%
He's, for heaven's sakes, five

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.566 size:78% position:39% line:92%
He's way ahead of me.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:14.534 line:92%
Not to mention the bicycle

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think around the same
time, ten,

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.904 line:92%
I started get on the bike.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.806 line:92%
He's whizzing around, you know

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're most precocious.
-And is he taking to the piano

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:24.744 size:84% position:42%
Do you feel like he has
a natural skill for it?

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:25.745 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, who knows?

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:26.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think he's
any Mozart, but --

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's no indication
of that, yet.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he's kinda like me,
disciplined.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.085 line:92%
It's around all the time.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.654
He sees me playing all the time,
so he likes to check in.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
We go through the stuff
and I'll be darned if he isn't

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:41.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, playing a bunch
of stuff! You know.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's thrilling for me.
-That's amazing.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's sometimes maddening
for me, too.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.233 line:92%
I'm very kind of, around piano

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get very [ Strikes hands ]
kind of, you know,

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not like the father
in "Shine."

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.072 line:92%
I'm not, you know, a maniac.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:56.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not gonna, you know, but..
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.578 line:92%
But I'm, you know, "Focus now.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:02:59.479 line:92%
I want him to be focused.

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:01.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a little tough,
but, you know,

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:02.549 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I think it's good.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:04.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's taking to it, yeah.
He's doing okay.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
The other one -- the other one
is taking little lessons.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:08.588 size:88% position:44% line:92%
River is taking lessons.

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:09.722 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Horrible, horrible.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:13.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
He comes in and all
I'm supposed to do is,

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
if he doesn't do anything,
which he doesn't,

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
is take his fingers
like a puppet

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:18.731 line:92%
and push them against the thing.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.734 size:84% position:42%
I play "Twinkle Twinkle
Little Star" every day

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:22.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
with his right hand,
his left hand,

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:26.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
as he's moaning and stuff,
and I just kinda do it.

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.408 size:81% position:41%
He says, "Do it quick,
as quick as you can,"

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause afterwards,
we give him Gummy Bears.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.278 size:88% position:44%
So that's what he likes.
-Oh, well, there you go.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to reward them,
somehow.

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:36.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd also like to say we've
been doing this show --

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.051
you know, we've done more
than a thousand of these

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:38.851 line:92%
and you're the first perso

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
to reference
the father in "Shine."

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:42.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I really appreciate
'cause I feel like

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:45.425
that's a cultural referenc
we've lost over the years.

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughing ]
-Oh, yeah, no.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:47.560 line:92%
We have to appeal to the kids.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
They love that "Shine"
stuff, yeah.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
-Call me a panderer,

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.465 line:92%
but I don't care, you know

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:55.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you like to play
to your teen base.

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:57.937 line:92%
Hey, I wanna ask about this.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:58.938 line:92%
I imagine one of the things --

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:02.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
again, it was
groundbreaking tech

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the first
"Jurassic Park" film

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, now, must seem
incredibly dated,

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:09.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think
you must look back.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were actually
pretty dangerous,

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.119 size:88% position:44% line:92%
the early T. rexes, yes?

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:14.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know what you're
talking about.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:15.321 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Well, not really.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's no such thing
as dinosaurs.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:19.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
-But, yes, it was
dangerous back then.

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:20.326 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The -- [ Laughs ]

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hate to be the one
to break it to you, you know

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:23.930 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-No, somebody had to.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, there's no Easter Bunny
either. No Easter Bunny.

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Aw, man.
-But, yeah, in the first one

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
Steven Spielberg,
if I can invoke his name,

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:33.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
was off-screen going,
"Rawr! Rawr!

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody look at the
tennis ball. Rawr! Rawr!"

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:37.744 size:88% position:44%
In this one, you know,
they have sound effects,

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:38.845 size:81% position:41% line:92%
so you hear dinosaurs.

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:41.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they've got
the big dinosaurs

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:42.048 line:92%
and it's great, you know.

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
But Stan Winston had,
back then,

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.685 line:92%
won the Oscar for what he did.

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:48.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, they were new,
they were groundbreaking

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.356 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and, on occasion,

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
there was T. rex
that was life-size,

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:54.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, when you went into the
sound stage, they said,

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.095 line:92%
"Don't go anywhere near it

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it can get
kind of --"

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.198 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and we're still trying

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
to figure out how
to operate it.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.037 size:84% position:42%
So it can go into kinda
unexpected convulsions

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:07.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
and [ Strikes palm ]
drop on you or attack you

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.241 size:78% position:39% line:92%
or it gets, you know.

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:09.042 line:92%
We didn't wanna get killed

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:11.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
by the fake T. rex,
so, you know.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:11.911 line:92%
-Yeah, that would've been --

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
certainly would've made
the press junket a lot harder,

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:17.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
if one of you had died
via the mechanical T. rex.

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:18.351 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-It would've been dour.

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:22.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
-It would've been dark days.

